================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY CREDITS AND ATTRIBUTION
================================================================================

Zyn Agent is an independent project. Its architecture was informed by several
excellent open-source agents, and credit belongs to their authors.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pi (pi-coding-agent)
Copyright (c) Mario Zechner (@badlogic) and Earendil Inc.
Licensed under the MIT License
https://github.com/earendil-works/pi

Zyn's core design follows Pi's minimalist philosophy: a small set of built-in
tools (read, write, edit, bash) with an agent loop that stays out of the way.
The four-tool model and the "extend rather than configure" approach come from
Pi's design. Mario Zechner is also the author of libGDX.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Zyn (original TUI, by SoyMaycol)
https://github.com/SoyMaycol/Zyn
https://github.com/toZyn/Zyn-Old

The terminal UI layout — themes, slash-command bar, spinner states and overall
composition — was inspired by this earlier Zyn TUI. Credit for the interface
concept belongs to its author.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OpenCode
Copyright (c) Anomaly (formerly SST)
Licensed under the MIT License
https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode

The provider catalog structure and the OpenCode Zen integration follow
OpenCode's model. Zen is used as Zyn's default provider for its free tier.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Claude Code (Anthropic) and Codex (OpenAI)
https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code
https://github.com/openai/codex

The SKILL.md format with YAML frontmatter, the `<available_skills>` prompt
block, and the handoff-document approach to context compaction follow the
conventions these agents established. Zyn implements compatible formats so
skills can be shared between tools.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Model Context Protocol (MCP)
Copyright (c) Anthropic
Licensed under the MIT License
https://modelcontextprotocol.io

Zyn implements an MCP stdio client and uses the same ~/.zyn/mcp.json server
definition format as other MCP-compatible tools.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
models.dev
https://models.dev

Context-window limits are sourced from the models.dev public API and cached
locally, so Zyn reports real limits rather than guesses.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES

Ink — Copyright (c) Vadim Demedes — MIT — https://github.com/vadimdemedes/ink
React — Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. — MIT — https://react.dev
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
